	p.fps = defaultFPS
} else if p.fps > maxFPS {
	p.fps = maxFPS
}
```

So out-of-range values are **silently clamped, not rejected**:

- `fps < 1` (zero, negative) → falls back to the default `60`
- `fps > 120` → capped at `120`
- Values `1`–`120` are used as-is

This matches the doc comment on `WithFPS` in `options.go`: *"If less than 1, the default value of 60 will be used. If over 120, the FPS will be capped at 120."*

